Subject: [PATCH 052/164] x86/virt/tdx: Add Secure EPT related SEAMCALL
 wrappers

Wire up SEAMCALL wrappers for Secure EPT (SEPT) related SEAMCALLs to:

 - Populate guest memory when creating the TDX guest.
 - Dynamically add private memory to TDX guest at runtime.
 - Zap private guest memory pages when moving/deleting memory slot.
 - Tear down private guest memory and SEPT tree when destroying guest.
 - Temporarily block/unblock Secure EPT mapping for private memory.
 - Handle TLB flush for SEPT mapping of guest private memory.

Signed-off-by: Isaku Yamahata <isaku.yamahata@intel.com>
Signed-off-by: Rick Edgecombe <rick.p.edgecombe@intel.com>

